# THE REGRESSION. `<https://::1>` is an IPv6 literal in the authority without
# the brackets RFC 3986/3987 require.
#
# In September 2026 a dump carrying this line passed the driver's gate and
# Oxigraph refused to load it. rete's classifier had no class for the defect —
# it has a scheme, no excluded character, no bracket (their ABSENCE is the
# defect), one '#', no '%' — so the unrepairable count read zero and the gate
# opened. #255 made validity the RFC 3987 parser's verdict rather than the
# classifier's, #256 made an independent parse required, and this file is what
# keeps both honest: a dataset containing this line must end `failed-invalid`
# and must NOT be uploaded.
<http://example.org/ok> <http://example.org/p> "a clean control" .
<http://example.org/ok> <http://example.org/rel> <http://example.org/also-fine> .
<https://::1> <http://example.org/p> "an IPv6 host that lost its brackets" .
